343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 321 0 R
/E (The music streaming sector has reshaped how audio content is produced, distributed, and consumed. Digital platforms have replaced physical ownership models with on-demand access, creating complex ecosystems that connect users, creators, rights holders, advertisers, and technology partners. Platforms such as Spotify operate as central coordinators within this ecosystem, enabling large-scale content distribution while facilitating monetisation, discovery, and data-driven engagement.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 321 0 R
/E (Rather than functioning as a traditional media distributor, the music streaming ecosystem is built around platform-based interactions, where value is created through network effects, algorithmic curation, and multi-sided revenue models. Spotify is used here as a representative case due to its global reach and mature platform infrastructure.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
